🔹 Built so far
• Adders: half adder, full adder, full adder from two half adders, 4-bit parallel adder (ripple carry), carry look-ahead, carry select and carry skip
• Subtractors: half subtractor, full subtractor and 4-bit parallel subtractor

🔹 What I learned
• A ripple carry adder is simple, but each carry waits for the stage before it, so it gets slower as the bits grow
• Carry look-ahead, carry select and carry skip are faster, because they trade extra hardware for speed
• Every design here was written in dataflow, structural and behavioral style
